    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job’s Opening Speech"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "After this, Job began to speak and cursed the day he was born."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He said:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "May the day I was born perish,",
          "and the night that said,",
          "“A boy is conceived.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If only that day had turned to darkness!",
          "May God above not care about it,",
          "or light shine on it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "May darkness and gloom reclaim it,",
          "and a cloud settle over it.",
          "May what darkens the day terrify it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If only darkness had taken that night away!",
          "May it not appear among the days of the year",
          "or be listed in the calendar."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Yes, may that night be barren;",
          "may no joyful shout be heard in it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let those who curse days",
          "condemn it,",
          "those who are ready to rouse Leviathan."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "May its morning stars grow dark.",
          "May it wait for daylight but have none;",
          "may it not see the breaking of dawn."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For that night did not shut",
          "the doors of my mother’s womb,",
          "and hide sorrow from my eyes."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why was I not stillborn;",
          "why didn’t I die as I came from the womb?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why did the knees receive me,",
          "and why were there breasts for me to nurse?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Now I would certainly be lying down in peace;",
          "I would be asleep.",
          "Then I would be at rest"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "with the kings and counselors of the earth,",
          "who rebuilt ruined cities for themselves,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "or with princes who had gold,",
          "who filled their houses with silver."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Or why was I not hidden like a miscarried child,",
          "like infants who never see daylight?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There the wicked cease to make trouble,",
          "and there the weary find rest."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The captives are completely at rest;",
          "they do not hear a taskmaster’s voice."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Both small and great are there,",
          "and the slave is set free from his master."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why is light given to one burdened with grief,",
          "and life to those whose existence is bitter,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "who wait for death, but it does not come,",
          "and search for it more than for hidden treasure,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "who are filled with much joy",
          "and are glad when they reach the grave?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why is life given to a man whose path is hidden,",
          "whom God has hedged in?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I sigh when food is put before me,",
          "and my groans pour out like water."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the thing I feared has overtaken me,",
          "and what I dreaded has happened to me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I cannot relax or be calm;",
          "I have no rest, for turmoil has come."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
